Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:41:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH v2] Cheap row-count-only instrumentation for EXPLAIN ANALYZE

When EXPLAIN ANALYZE runs with TIMING OFF and BUFFERS OFF (and no WAL
usage), the only per-node statistic needed is the row count.  Until now
such nodes still went through ExecProcNodeInstr() for every tuple.

Instead, count rows on the caller's side in the inline ExecProcNode().
The flag, the "running" state and the counter are packed into a single
uint64 in PlanState (instr_rows), located next to the ExecProcNode
pointer, so the per-tuple cost is one load, one test and one store, and
no individual ExecXXX node function needs to know about it.  The packed
counter is folded into the node's NodeInstrumentation by the new
ExecInstrEndLoop(), which replaces the existing InstrEndLoop() calls on
plan nodes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UovmohnnszTFF6bbcaFDhU
